00:09:49.865 --> 00:09:51.740
CORNELIUS WILLIS: So
you got both the earring

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.650
posts and the superglue
at the same store.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.740
NEAL MUELLER: Same place, yeah.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:54.910
CORNELIUS WILLIS: Wow.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.014
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Very useful.

00:09:56.014 --> 00:09:57.388
CORNELIUS WILLIS:
Very efficient.

00:09:57.388 --> 00:10:00.200
So he came back with the
studs and convinced him

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.740
that it would be something
that would really get

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.450
his picture in a lot of places.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.890
NEAL MUELLER: And could
potentially glue his ear

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:07.890
together with superglue.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:08.848
CORNELIUS WILLIS: Yeah.

00:10:08.848 --> 00:10:10.850
And the thing that I think
we were excited about

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.960
is figuring out how to
actually map this down

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.387
into Urs's own sort
of immune system.

00:10:16.387 --> 00:10:18.470
So it's just the same way
we have an immune system

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.240
for our cloud, maybe
we could figure out

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.080
how to make that connection.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:22.860
MARK MANDEL: I'm a
little sad, actually.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.235
